      "writtenOn": "2024-03-11T21:49:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was hoping to do it statically. This seems like a good spot, because it\u0027s a boundary between the natural Zephyr type for this information and our legacy type. Everywhere else is only in terms of one type.\n\nThere\u0027s actually `ATOMIC_DEFINE` that creates an array of `atomic_t` big enough to store a specified number of bits. Hypothetically, this whole API could be defined in terms of a portably big enough object flag array. I started trying to use that to ensure that the events object was big enough to hold the number of events that we have, but I couldn\u0027t figure out the idiomatic way to then access the object without repeating the size calculation, and it seemed like it was going to end up being very verbose anyway.",
